[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Life on a Desert Island]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.49]Lesson 12 | 第12课
[00:02.27]Life on a desert island | 荒岛生活
[00:09.61]What was exceptional about the two men's stay on the desert island? | 这两个人在荒岛上的逗留有什么特别之处？
[00:16.24]Most of us have formed an unrealistic picture of life on a desert island. | 我们许多人对荒岛生活抱有不切实际的想象。
[00:22.19]We sometimes imagine a desert island to be a sort of paradise where the sun always shines. | 我们有时把荒岛想象成一个阳光终日普照的乐园。
[00:29.85]Life there is simple and good. | 那里的生活简单而美好。
[00:32.44]Ripe fruit falls from the trees and you never have to work. | 熟了的果子从树上掉下来，人们从来无需劳作。
[00:37.52]The other side of the picture is quite the opposite. | 另一种想象恰恰相反。
[00:41.16]Life on a desert island is wretched. | 荒岛生活很凄惨。
[00:43.94]You either starve to death or live like Robinson Crusoe, waiting for a boat which never comes. | 你要么饿死，要么像鲁滨逊·克鲁索那样生活，盼着一艘永远等不来的船。
[00:52.49]Perhaps there is an element of truth in both these pictures, but few of us have had the opportunity to find out. | 也许这两种想象都含有一定的真实成分，但我们当中很少有人有机会去弄个明白。
[01:00.81]Two men who recently spent five days on a coral island wished they had stayed there longer. | 最近在珊瑚岛上待了5天的两个人真希望当时能再多待些日子。
[01:09.25]They were taking a badly damaged boat from the Virgin Islands to Miami to have it repaired. | 他们驾着一条严重损坏的船从维尔京群岛去迈阿密修理。
[01:15.85]During the journey, their boat began to sink. | 途中，船开始下沉。
[01:20.15]They quickly loaded a small rubber dinghy with food, matches, and cans of beer and rowed for a few miles across the Caribbean until they arrived at a tiny coral island. | 他们迅速把食物、火柴和几罐啤酒装上一只橡皮救生筏，划过加勒比海的几英里水面，来到一座小小的珊瑚岛上。
[01:33.63]There were hardly any trees on the island and there was no water, but this did not prove to be a problem. | 岛上几乎没有树木，也没有淡水，但这并没有构成什么问题。
[01:41.52]The men collected rainwater in the rubber dinghy. | 他们用橡皮筏收集雨水。
[01:45.28]As they had brought a spear gun with them, they had plenty to eat. | 由于他们随身带了一支捕鱼枪，吃的东西绰绰有余。
[01:49.56]They caught lobster and fish every day, and as one of them put it 'ate like kings'. | 他们天天捕鱼捉龙虾，正如其中一人所说，“吃得像国王一样”。
[01:57.20]When a passing tanker rescued them five days later, both men were genuinely sorry that they had to leave. | 5天后，一艘路过的油轮把他们救走时，两个人都真心为不得不离开而感到遗憾。
